## What's NOT audited

For transparency, these are intentional limitations:

- **C library behavior.** We audit the Rust↔C boundary; we don't audit the C library itself (we cite its documented contracts).
- **OS-level guarantees.** We rely on libc / POSIX / kernel docs without re-verifying them.
- **External crates' soundness.** We audit our USE of them; we trust their internal audits (versions pinned per Cargo.lock).
- **Inverse-fuzzing coverage gaps.** We fuzz the highest-risk pub fns; some lower-risk surfaces are not fuzzed.
- **Formal verification.** Most sites use property tests + miri; only the highest-stakes sites have kani proofs.

To extend coverage, see [the audit dir's CONTRIBUTING.md] or contact <SECURITY_EMAIL>.

